  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1201 AM MDT Wed Aug 19 2026\n\nFrom Thursday into early next week, the ridge aloft will generally \nremain just south of CO. It will wobble a bit to the west and east, \nbut overall it will generally be over the region. Moisture is \ntrapped under this ridge, and this will allow for a pattern of \nafternoon and evening thunderstorm activity over the region during \nthe period. Overall best chance of storms will be over the higher \nterrain, with more isolated to scattered storms over the plains. The \nwarmest days will likely occur this weekend, where temps will be \nat or around 100F over parts of the plains.\n\nGiven the fact that we will likely see storms over the higher \nterrain each day, flash flooding can not be ruled out over the burn \nscars. Any storm which produces locally heavy rain which develops \nover the burn scars will have the capability of producing flash \nflooding. \\/Hodanish",
